Save93 / Whiterun exterior / DynDOLOD root-lock release and stock tasklet admission / 2026-11-09

Setup and methods
- Skyrim AE 1.6.1170.0, exact Save93 copy, SSE Display Tweaks 0.5.16 with its 42 FPS cap and dynamic Papyrus budget, frame generation off only in the disposable fixture. Four Bannered Mare to WhiterunWorld transitions and 32 Utility.Wait(0.01) probes per window. Observation only.
- For GetWorldSpace calls whose queue wait overlaps the final DynDOLOD stack's root-lock wait, match native completion, the stock return-tasklet enqueue bracket (R/r), and acceptance (T) by exact tasklet pointer and stack. Pair that pointer to the real submitted BSJobs list and preceding stock collection call. Count a missed collection only when the entire enqueue finished before an earlier stock collection start. A publication overlapping collection is reported separately.
- Capture the stock caller RVA immediately after the existing atomic object release succeeds on a DynDOLOD root in VMProcess. Match the same lock token through acquisition and release and correlate the subsequent different-object acquisition and next delayed native dispatch. The verified release call at 104853+0x29F returns to RVA 0x144E614. The original code compares previous and next script-object pointers and releases the old object's lock only on the different-object branch before attempting the new lock.
- Time the existing TasksToJobs vtable method 104855 and compare the job array capacity before and after the original method. Every real submitted tasklet list is checked against the actual size delta. Array growth is the diagnostic criterion for the preallocation candidate. Elapsed time in the whole method is a conservative upper bound on time that its own optimization could save per call.
- Also examined the operation-limit mechanism in Papyrus Tweaks NG (https://github.com/Nightfallstorm/PapyrusTweaks/blob/main/src/hooks/performance/MaxOps.h). It raises the operation count in the bytecode loop. Here an extra instruction budget could matter only if a resumed tasklet yielded again before the lock switch.
- Test DLL built and runtime installation passed. Budget policy and synthetic collection boundary, capacity, job membership and next-call pairing checks passed. Final DLL SHA256 BB532DB496AF81BB1C2452CD0E7BEB89416C58FD2DA315085F32A3C81D7D92F4. Raw capture build/gameplay-trace/cell-42-getworldspace-release-observe.

